cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use KESTREL (formerly PlanetFinder) or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "KESTREL: an independent search of TESS light curves for transiting planets around bright K and M dwarfs"
authors:
  - family-names: Price
    given-names: Steve
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6010-3869"
abstract: >-
  An unattended pipeline that searches TESS light curves (SPOC, TESS-SPOC and QLP)
  for transiting planets around bright, lightly observed K and M dwarfs, with automated
  vetting: odd/even, secondary-eclipse, uniqueness and duration tests, pixel-level
  position checks and per-source pixel depth maps, independent-reduction checks, a physical transit fit with a
  stellar-density test, and TRICERATOPS false-positive probabilities. Candidates are
  published with their evidence at https://github.com/moosesteve21/PlanetCandidates.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - transit search
  - TESS
  - M dwarfs
  - K dwarfs
  - vetting
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/moosesteve21/PlanetFinder"
type: software
